  "summary_en": "Section 21a of the German Air Traffic Act designates the Federal Aviation Office as competent authority for remote pilot competency exams and certificates in the EU 'open' drone category, assigns operational oversight to state aviation authorities, and permits fully automated issuance of certificates and fee notices with safeguards for human review.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Luftfahrt-Bundesamt is competent authority for remote pilot exams and certificates in the open category.",
   "Exam candidates must present valid ID and, if minors, guardian consent.",
   "State aviation authorities supervise open-category UAS operations.",
   "Certificates and fee notices may be issued fully automatically.",
   "Remote pilots keep the right to be heard and to a decision by an official."
